      "side": 1,
      "message": "Why is this implemented as a StrictMode check instead of being done directly in libcore/ as part of the ZipFile implementation ?",
      "revId": "8cd51716afbce907cb555f81d5705bfc0d712035",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "e0b84d33_7a3461bb",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 10
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 1071150
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-09-27T11:04:02Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The earlier implementation in libcore was changing behaviour on debug vs non-debug and using log.wtf() and seemingly open to more policy controls (potentially enabling for priv apps only). Since we don\u0027t ever want this in libcore, the suggestion was to move the check into frameworks.\n\nIf there aren\u0027t going to be policy quirks, okay to move back there.",
      "parentUuid": "032562ea_50f51fb8",
      "revId": "8cd51716afbce907cb555f81d5705bfc0d712035",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "8ddb7555_047eed3d",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 10
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 1014443
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-09-27T11:10:22Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "ChangeIds are available on libcore, as is VMRuntime...getTargetSdkVersion() so i don\u0027t see why not ? StrictMode is an odd place to add this, IMO.",
      "parentUuid": "e0b84d33_7a3461bb",
      "revId": "8cd51716afbce907cb555f81d5705bfc0d712035",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "a9066fe9_2183c5e1",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 10
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 1133744
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-09-27T11:15:37Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "From Dianne\u0027s recommendation we\u0027ll also want to log this to WW (as opposed to initially Log.wtf) regardless of `targetSdk`, but that will come later. Code in `onPathAccess()` (http://cs/android/frameworks/base/core/java/android/os/StrictMode.java;l\u003d1911-1929;rcl\u003db82b6808e11412efa48034f5296acc55703fc492) seems to be similar to what we\u0027re doing. Would you still prefer this in libcore, Narayan?",
      "parentUuid": "8ddb7555_047eed3d",
      "revId": "8cd51716afbce907cb555f81d5705bfc0d712035",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "17258fe3_089949d3",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 10
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 1133744
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-09-27T11:21:19Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Ah, if we moved to libcore we\u0027d also need to gate on the OS version. My understanding is that we get that for free by implementing `onZipEntryAccess()` here in `frameworks/base`.",
      "parentUuid": "a9066fe9_2183c5e1",
      "revId": "8cd51716afbce907cb555f81d5705bfc0d712035",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "0f11c67b_234e44f1",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 10
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 1071150
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-09-28T11:02:25Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The preferred method for API behaviour changes in libcore is to gate on both the targetSDK and the platform version (*). libcore is pushed via mainline so a U change in libcore will end up on an S device and we can\u0027t do (adequate) retrospective compat testing on S. We generally try not to change existing API behaviour in libcore. \n\nThere\u0027s no such double checking needed if this change is in frameworks. If you push a little harder to expose this in StrictMode you could allow people to opt-out of this behaviour change if they\u0027ve implemented their own ZIP path checks (go/aakb/zip-path-traversal) and path fix-ups.\n\nSimilarly if you end up with any policy that requires frameworks knowledge then having a frameworks part is useful as libcore knows little about the code above it.",
      "parentUuid": "17258fe3_089949d3",
      "revId": "8cd51716afbce907cb555f81d5705bfc0d712035",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    }
